{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfXH2hdtAx9tXAR7FXJEB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N1mB5uXxZZufMsajPN6Pc7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Setoid/Subalgebras.lagda.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":10188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":350},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e92d852-75c7-4eb2-846a-0a3ab8fc98cc","uuid":"a1a1034e-b65c-403a-ac7d-db01ed8a4951","timestamp":"2026-09-29T06:43:28.697Z","request_id":"req_011CfXH2h9c4RmZB4epuGSzm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01N1mB5uXxZZufMsajPN6Pc7":{"file_path":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Setoid/Subalgebras.lagda.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N1mB5uXxZZufMsajPN6Pc7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tlayout: default\n3\ttitle : \"Setoid.Subalgebras module (The Agda Universal Algebra Library)\"\n4\tdate : \"2021-07-26\"\n5\tauthor: \"agda-algebras development team\"\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t### Subalgebras over setoids\n9\t\n10\tThis is the [Setoid.Subalgebras][] module of the [Agda Universal Algebra Library][].\n11\t\n12\tThis is a barrel module: it declares nothing of its own and re-exports the five\n13\tmodules that make up the theory of subalgebras over setoids.\n14\t\n15\tIn this library, we call an algebra `𝑨` a **subalgebra** of `𝑩`, written `𝑨 ≤ 𝑩`,\n16\tprovided `𝑨` can be homomorphically embedded in `𝑩`, that is, when some\n17\thomomorphism from `𝑨` to `𝑩` has an injective underlying map.  This is not the\n18\tstandard textbook definition, but is essentially (*algebraically*) equivalent to\n19\tit.\n20\t\n21\tNormally one defines a **subuniverse** to be a subset of the carrier of an algebra\n22\tthat is closed under the operations; a subalgebra is then a subuniverse\n23\ttogether with the operations of the larger algebra restricted to it.\n24\tWe *do* define subuniverses in the standard way in the\n25\t[Setoid.Subalgebras.Subuniverses][] module, so the textbook definition of\n26\tsubalgebra is available to us.  But the homomorphic embedding interpretation of\n27\tthe subalgebra relation turns out to be more convenient for our purposes.\n28\t\n29\tTaking subalgebras is one of the three closure operations whose composite defines\n30\ta variety, and `S`{.AgdaFunction} of [Setoid.Varieties.Closure][] is defined\n31\tdirectly in terms of the `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction} introduced here.\n32\t\n33\t#### Guide to the submodules of <span class=\"AgdaModule\">Setoid.Subalgebras</span>\n34\t\n35\t+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Basic][]: the relation `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction}, its converse\n36\t   `_≥_`{.AgdaFunction}, the bundled `SubalgebraOf`{.AgdaRecord} and\n37\t   `Subalgebra`{.AgdaFunction} forms, the class-relative `_≤c_`{.AgdaFunction},\n38\t   and `mon→≤`{.AgdaFunction};\n39\t+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Properties][]: that `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction} is a preorder,\n40\t   which is as far as it goes (mutual embeddings do not yield an isomorphism in\n41\t   general, though they do for finite algebras); how `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction}\n42\t   interacts with isomorphism and with universe lifting; and that it is preserved\n43\t   by products;\n44\t+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Subuniverses][]: the subsets of a carrier closed under the\n45\t   operations, the subuniverse they generate, and the induction principle that\n46\t   makes generation usable;\n47\t+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.CompleteLattice][]: the subuniverses of a fixed algebra,\n48\t   ordered by inclusion, as a complete lattice;\n49\t+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Subdirect][]: subdirect products, subdirect\n50\t   irreducibility, and Birkhoff's subdirect representation theorem, which is\n51\t   proved relative to a choice principle in general and unconditionally for\n52\t   finite algebras.\n53\t\n54\t```agda\n55\t{-# OPTIONS --cubical-compatible --exact-split --safe #-}\n56\t\n57\tmodule Setoid.Subalgebras where\n58\t\n59\topen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Basic public\n60\topen import Setoid.Subalgebras.CompleteLattice public\n61\topen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Properties public\n62\topen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Subuniverses public\n63\topen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Subdirect public\n64\t```\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e92d852-75c7-4eb2-846a-0a3ab8fc98cc","uuid":"efe122fe-8012-4908-9952-1c54668bf8c1","timestamp":"2026-09-29T06:43:28.703Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Setoid/Subalgebras.lagda.md","content":"---\nlayout: default\ntitle : \"Setoid.Subalgebras module (The Agda Universal Algebra Library)\"\ndate : \"2021-07-26\"\nauthor: \"agda-algebras development team\"\n---\n\n### Subalgebras over setoids\n\nThis is the [Setoid.Subalgebras][] module of the [Agda Universal Algebra Library][].\n\nThis is a barrel module: it declares nothing of its own and re-exports the five\nmodules that make up the theory of subalgebras over setoids.\n\nIn this library, we call an algebra `𝑨` a **subalgebra** of `𝑩`, written `𝑨 ≤ 𝑩`,\nprovided `𝑨` can be homomorphically embedded in `𝑩`, that is, when some\nhomomorphism from `𝑨` to `𝑩` has an injective underlying map.  This is not the\nstandard textbook definition, but is essentially (*algebraically*) equivalent to\nit.\n\nNormally one defines a **subuniverse** to be a subset of the carrier of an algebra\nthat is closed under the operations; a subalgebra is then a subuniverse\ntogether with the operations of the larger algebra restricted to it.\nWe *do* define subuniverses in the standard way in the\n[Setoid.Subalgebras.Subuniverses][] module, so the textbook definition of\nsubalgebra is available to us.  But the homomorphic embedding interpretation of\nthe subalgebra relation turns out to be more convenient for our purposes.\n\nTaking subalgebras is one of the three closure operations whose composite defines\na variety, and `S`{.AgdaFunction} of [Setoid.Varieties.Closure][] is defined\ndirectly in terms of the `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction} introduced here.\n\n#### Guide to the submodules of <span class=\"AgdaModule\">Setoid.Subalgebras</span>\n\n+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Basic][]: the relation `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction}, its converse\n   `_≥_`{.AgdaFunction}, the bundled `SubalgebraOf`{.AgdaRecord} and\n   `Subalgebra`{.AgdaFunction} forms, the class-relative `_≤c_`{.AgdaFunction},\n   and `mon→≤`{.AgdaFunction};\n+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Properties][]: that `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction} is a preorder,\n   which is as far as it goes (mutual embeddings do not yield an isomorphism in\n   general, though they do for finite algebras); how `_≤_`{.AgdaFunction}\n   interacts with isomorphism and with universe lifting; and that it is preserved\n   by products;\n+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Subuniverses][]: the subsets of a carrier closed under the\n   operations, the subuniverse they generate, and the induction principle that\n   makes generation usable;\n+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.CompleteLattice][]: the subuniverses of a fixed algebra,\n   ordered by inclusion, as a complete lattice;\n+  [Setoid.Subalgebras.Subdirect][]: subdirect products, subdirect\n   irreducibility, and Birkhoff's subdirect representation theorem, which is\n   proved relative to a choice principle in general and unconditionally for\n   finite algebras.\n\n```agda\n{-# OPTIONS --cubical-compatible --exact-split --safe #-}\n\nmodule Setoid.Subalgebras where\n\nopen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Basic public\nopen import Setoid.Subalgebras.CompleteLattice public\nopen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Properties public\nopen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Subuniverses public\nopen import Setoid.Subalgebras.Subdirect public\n```\n","numLines":65,"startLine":1,"totalLines":65}}}
